==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|lumpe|lang=enm}}. Confer {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Lumpen||lang=de|rag}} and {{term|Lump||lang=de|ragamuffin}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-lump.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ʌmp|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Something that [[protrudes]], sticks out, or sticks together; a [[cluster]] or [[blob]]; a [[mound]], [[hill]], or [[group]].
#: ''Stir the gravy until there are no more '''lumps'''.''
#: ''a '''lump''' of coal; a '''lump''' of clay; a '''lump''' of cheese''
# A group, [[set]], or [[unit]].
#: ''The money arrived all at once as one big '''lump''' sum payment.''
# A small, shaped mass of sugar, typically about a teaspoonful.
#: ''Do you want one '''lump''' or two with your coffee?''
# A dull or lazy person.
#: ''Don't just sit there like a '''lump'''.''
# {{context|informal|as plural|lang=en}} A beating or verbal abuse.
#: ''He's taken his '''lumps''' over the years.''
#* {{quote-book|title=The cold war on the periphery: the United States, India, and Pakistan|page=323|author=Robert J. McMahon|year=1994|passage=Komer admitted that the United States would probably suffer "short term '''lumps'''" as a result of Johnson's brusque decision.}}
# A [[projection]] beneath the [[breech]] end of a [[gun]] [[barrel]].

